Metal backend: menu, key events, anti-aliasing and window handling.

- A main menu with a "Quit <title>" item; like Cmd+Q (the toolkit's, #544) it ends the game through ps3_host_quit.
- The window drops key down/up events (the pad polls the keyboard itself), so a keypress no longer plays the
  system alert sound.
- Anisotropic filtering of linearly filtered textures on the old live-draw path (PS3RECOMP_METAL_AF=1..16, default
  16); the draw engine uses the toolkit's own PS3_AA / PS3_SHARPEN / PS3_ANISO. PS3RECOMP_METAL_HEADLESS=1 with
  PS3RECOMP_METAL_PRESENT_DUMP=<dir> writes every 120th presented frame.
- The window is resizable without stretching: the drawable follows the window in device pixels and the display
  pass fits the 16:9 picture into it, black elsewhere. PS3RECOMP_METAL_WINDOW=WxH sets the initial size.

---

